sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Authorizer A
    participant B as Authorizer B
    participant PG as Project PostgreSQL database
    participant OAuth as External OAuth provider
    Note over A,B: Same project + credential configuration; local token missing/expired
    A->>PG: Read shared token
    PG-->>A: Missing / expired
    B->>PG: Read shared token
    PG-->>B: Missing / expired
    A->>PG: Conditional UPDATE: claim 12 s lease, version++
    PG-->>A: Owner UUID + version v
    B->>PG: Conditional lease claim
    PG-->>B: No row updated: lease already held
    Note over A,PG: No SQL transaction/connection held across OAuth call
    A->>OAuth: HTTPS client_credentials; 8 s timeout
    OAuth-->>A: Derived token + lifetime
    A->>A: Safe reuse deadline = now + TTL - min(TTL / 10, 30 s)
    A->>A: AES-256-GCM encrypt {value, expires}; AAD = id/version
    A->>PG: Publish WHERE owner/version match AND lease valid
    PG-->>A: Committed shared token; release lease
    loop Until state is ready or request times out
        B->>PG: Re-read shared state
        PG-->>B: Pending or token version v
        B->>B: If pending, wait 100 ms
    end
    B->>B: Decrypt token version v; cache locally
    Note over A,B: On token use: memory if last check < 1 s ago; otherwise SQL. No idle polling or pub-sub.
    Note over A,PG: Acquisition error: release lease + shared 2 s cooldown
    Note over A,PG: Explicit invalidation increments version and clears token + lease
    Note over A,PG: Crash: lease expires; late or superseded publication rejected
    Note over A,OAuth: External login cannot be exactly once across a crash
